<ContentPage xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui" xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml" xmlns:vm="clr-namespace:CafePosApp.ViewModels" x:Class="CafePosApp.Views.ShiftAnalyticsPage" x:DataType="vm:ShiftAnalyticsViewModel" Title="Аналитика смены"
             Shell.NavBarIsVisible="False">
    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
         ФИЛЬТРЫ, СОРТИРОВКА, ГРУППИРОВКА — seven controls for one list.

         The reasons are recorded rather than the layout being "obvious":

         1. THE LIST IS THREE COLLECTIONS, NOT ONE. ProductAnalyticsProjection returns whichever
            shape the grouping asks for, and a BindableLayout cannot pick a DataTemplate by runtime
            type. Three trees, one of them visible, bound to three flags — not a union row type with
            IsVisible panels, which would have meant one template rendering three different things.

         2. ISGrouped IS NOT AN OPTION HERE. XamlC cannot resolve PropertyGroupDescription, so
            CollectionView.IsGrouped is a Debug-only green build and a Release failure (XC0000) —
            the same trap OrdersPage documents at line 151. The headers are ordinary rows.

         3. THE PANEL IS CLOSED BY DEFAULT, and its trigger carries the current state IN WORDS. The
            cards at the top of this page do not change when the list is filtered, so a trigger that
            only read «Фильтры и сортировка» would leave the reader unable to tell a filtered list
            from an unfiltered one.

         4. TOUCH TARGETS ARE 44-48dp THROUGHOUT (§6). The chips reuse the shared FilterChip style
            the catalogue and the orders board use, so the three strips read as one control family.
         ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <!-- Same verdict as the shift report, same reason, same history: this page HAD a
         ScrollView and it was deliberately REMOVED to give the product breakdown a recycling
         CollectionView on the only `*` row. The consequence was arithmetic, and it is the bug
         the owner reported:
         ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
         EVERY Auto ROW ABOVE THE `*` WAS PAID FOR OUT OF THE LIST.

         With a counted shift selected, in portrait on a 411x914dp screen, «Продажи по блюдам и
         модификаторам» measured low=826dp and the tab bar began at 867dp — the list had zero
         height. No rows, and nothing to scroll. The same screen with the reconciliation card
         hidden rendered two product rows, which is exactly why it looked fine until the card
         appeared, and worse on a real device with a shorter viewport.

         So: one ScrollView, and the list renders its FULL content inside it. A CollectionView
         inside a ScrollView needs an explicit HeightRequest guessed from an item count — wrong
         today, a maintenance trap the next time a row changes height — so the list is a
         BindableLayout on a VerticalStackLayout: the idiom already used on the shift report, on
         SettingsPage and on the catalogue forms. One scroller, one gesture, and the list measures
         itself, so NO part of this layout depends on the height left over. A short phone,
         landscape and a tall one behave the same.

         The trade-off, stated rather than discovered later: nothing on this list recycles. It
         is bounded — the distinct products, modifiers and variants sold in ONE shift — so
         rendering it whole is affordable.

         The remark that used to sit here — that a dedicated row for the reconciliation card
         would quietly cost 10dp of list height, because GridLayoutManager.SumDefinitions adds
         RowSpacing for every index above the first regardless of whether the row has a visible
         child (dotnet/maui#11222) — is still true about hidden Grid rows, and the card is still
         stacked rather than boxed for the second reason: VerticalStackLayout really does cost
         nothing, because its measure loop `continue`s over a collapsed child and counts it in
         neither the height nor the spacing count. What it no longer buys is list HEIGHT, which is
         why a dedicated row is no longer off the table.
         ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <ScrollView>
        <Grid RowDefinitions="Auto,Auto,Auto,Auto,Auto,Auto,Auto,Auto,Auto,Auto" Padding="16" RowSpacing="10">
            <!-- The shift picker, full width. It used to share a row with «Обновить», which
                 is gone by the owner's decision: this page has no polling, so the button was
                 its only manual reload and OnAppearing is now the way to refresh — leaving the
                 page and coming back reloads it. «Обновить аналитику» below is NOT the same
                 control and stays: that one re-runs the analysis for the currently selected
                 shift without leaving the page, which is the point of the page. -->
            <Picker Title="Смена" ItemsSource="{Binding Shifts}" ItemDisplayBinding="{Binding DisplayName}" SelectedItem="{Binding SelectedShift}" VerticalOptions="Center" />
            <!-- Static value, so an AppThemeBinding on the attribute is the whole fix and needs no ViewModel
                 change. A bare {StaticResource Danger} declared the light token in both themes: on
                 the page fill (#FAFAFA / #121212) that is 4.77:1 in light and 3.76:1 in dark,
                 against the 4.5:1 owed at 14pt. DangerDark #FF9E8E on #121212 is 9.40:1. -->
            <Label Grid.Row="1" Text="{Binding Message}" IsVisible="{Binding HasMessage}"
                   TextColor="{AppThemeBinding Light={StaticResource Danger}, Dark={StaticResource DangerDark}}"
                   LineBreakMode="WordWrap" />
                <Button Grid.Row="2" Text="Обновить аналитику" Command="{Binding AnalyzeCommand}" />
                <!-- Ten cells in five rows. The two new ones are the MONEY the shift's revenue is made
                     of: a manager holding a reconciled cash figure next to an unreconcilable total
                     cannot answer "did the till balance" — the owner's actual question — because the
                     other half of the money is not on the page. Cash is the net (the count in the
                     drawer); card is the net too, with the refunds that produced it in a caption, so
                     the two can be added up against «Выручка» without guessing which is gross. -->
                <Grid Grid.Row="3" ColumnDefinitions="*,*" RowDefinitions="Auto,Auto,Auto,Auto,Auto" ColumnSpacing="10" RowSpacing="10">
                    <Border Style="{StaticResource CardBorder}"><VerticalStackLayout><Label Text="Выручка" Style="{StaticResource SecondaryLabel}" /><Label Text="{Binding RevenueText}" FontSize="18" FontAttributes="Bold" /></VerticalStackLayout></Border>
                    <Border Grid.Column="1" Style="{StaticResource CardBorder}"><VerticalStackLayout><Label Text="Заказов" Style="{StaticResource SecondaryLabel}" /><Label Text="{Binding OrdersCount}" FontSize="18" FontAttributes="Bold" /></VerticalStackLayout></Border>
                    <Border Grid.Row="1" Style="{StaticResource CardBorder}"><VerticalStackLayout><Label Text="Средний чек" Style="{StaticResource SecondaryLabel}" /><Label Text="{Binding AverageCheckText}" FontSize="18" FontAttributes="Bold" /></VerticalStackLayout></Border>
                    <Border Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="1" Style="{StaticResource CardBorder}"><VerticalStackLayout><Label Text="Продано позиций" Style="{StaticResource SecondaryLabel}" /><Label Text="{Binding ItemsCount}" FontSize="18" FontAttributes="Bold" /></VerticalStackLayout></Border>
                    <Border Grid.Row="2" Style="{StaticResource CardBorder}"><VerticalStackLayout><Label Text="Среднее приготовление" Style="{StaticResource SecondaryLabel}" /><Label Text="{Binding AveragePreparationTime}" FontSize="16" FontAttributes="Bold" /></VerticalStackLayout></Border>
                    <Border Grid.Row="2" Grid.Column="1" Style="{StaticResource CardBorder}"><VerticalStackLayout><Label Text="Среднее выполнение" Style="{StaticResource SecondaryLabel}" /><Label Text="{Binding AverageCompletionTime}" FontSize="16" FontAttributes="Bold" /></VerticalStackLayout></Border>
                    <Border Grid.Row="3" Style="{StaticResource CardBorder}"><VerticalStackLayout><Label Text="Всего заказов" Style="{StaticResource SecondaryLabel}" /><Label Text="{Binding AllOrdersCount}" FontSize="18" FontAttributes="Bold" /></VerticalStackLayout></Border>
                    <Border Grid.Row="3" Grid.Column="1" Style="{StaticResource CardBorder}"><VerticalStackLayout><Label Text="Отменено" Style="{StaticResource SecondaryLabel}" /><Label Text="{Binding CancelledOrdersCount}" FontSize="18" FontAttributes="Bold" /></VerticalStackLayout></Border>
                    <Border Grid.Row="4" Style="{StaticResource CardBorder}">
                        <VerticalStackLayout>
                            <Label Text="Наличные в кассе" Style="{StaticResource SecondaryLabel}" />
                            <!-- The description rides on the VALUE, not on the Border: a container with a
                                 contentDescription is announced as a single node and its children stop
                                 being traversed, so putting it on the card would cost a screen reader
                                 both labels to explain one number. -->
                            <Label Text="{Binding CashInDrawerText}" FontSize="18" FontAttributes="Bold"
                                   SemanticProperties.Description="Наличные в кассе: внесён размен плюс принято наличными, минус возвращено наличными и изъято на инкассацию" />

                            <!-- The two terms of that total that are not orders, under it. A manager
                                 reading this card for a CLOSED shift has no other screen that can
                                 tell them whether a shortage was change nobody put in or a
                                 collection nobody recorded, and the answer decides what they go and
                                 look for. -->
                            <Label Text="{Binding FloatCashText, StringFormat='Размен: {0}'}"
                                   Style="{StaticResource SecondaryLabel}" FontSize="12" />
                            <Label Text="{Binding PayoutCashText, StringFormat='Изъято: {0}'}"
                                   Style="{StaticResource SecondaryLabel}" FontSize="12" />
                        </VerticalStackLayout>
                    </Border>
                    <Border Grid.Row="4" Grid.Column="1" Style="{StaticResource CardBorder}">
                        <VerticalStackLayout>
                            <Label Text="Картой" Style="{StaticResource SecondaryLabel}" />
                            <Label Text="{Binding CardTotalText}" FontSize="18" FontAttributes="Bold"
                                   SemanticProperties.Description="Картой, за вычетом возвратов" />
                            <Label Text="{Binding CardRefundsText}" Style="{StaticResource CountLabel}" IsVisible="{Binding HasCardRefunds}" />
                        </VerticalStackLayout>
                    </Border>
                </Grid>
                <!-- Two cards, one page row. Spacing 10 mirrors the Grid's RowSpacing so the rhythm is
                     unchanged when both are visible, and a hidden child costs neither height nor
                     spacing — see the note at the top. -->
                <VerticalStackLayout Grid.Row="4" Spacing="10">
                    <Border Style="{StaticResource CardBorder}">
                        <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="4">
                            <Label Text="Пиковый час" FontAttributes="Bold" />
                            <Label Text="{Binding PeakHour}" Style="{StaticResource SecondaryLabel}" />
                        </VerticalStackLayout>
                    </Border>
                    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
                         ПЕРЕСЧЁТ КАССЫ — the recorded count of THIS shift, and the reason this screen
                         is its only home. The shift report cannot show it: that page rebinds to the new
                         shift after a close and carries no shift id in its route, so it can only ever
                         display the open shift, which by definition has no count. A block there would
                         have been permanently invisible.
    
                         Four rules on what is rendered:
                           1. No bare signed number, ever. "-240,00" alone is ambiguous in Russian — as
                              a delta it is a shortage, as a balance it is an overdraft — so the
                              direction lives in the sentence (Сходится / Не хватает … / Лишние …) and
                              the amount is printed unsigned. See CashWording.
                           2. The expectation always carries its moment. A bare "Ожидалось" is a claim
                              about an unspecified drawer, and read a week later it cannot be used.
                           3. Never a counted zero. A shift that was not counted yields no card at all,
                              which is a different fact from a drawer that came out empty.
                           4. Colour is the third signal, never the first: the word carries the state,
                              the tint only repeats it, and a screen reader is handed the phrase.
                         ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
                    <Border Style="{StaticResource CardBorder}" IsVisible="{Binding HasReconciliation}">
                        <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="4">
                            <!-- Same title treatment as «Пиковый час» above it: two cards stacked on one
                                 page row that styled their headings differently would read as two
                                 unrelated systems. The emphasis belongs on the difference line. -->
                            <Label Text="Пересчёт кассы" FontAttributes="Bold" />
                            <Label Text="{Binding CountedAtText}" Style="{StaticResource SecondaryLabel}" />
                            <Label Text="{Binding ExpectedAtCloseText}" />
                            <Label Text="{Binding CountedText}" />
                            <!-- The description is on the difference line, NOT on the card: a container
                                 with a contentDescription is announced as one node and its children are
                                 not traversed, so it would hide the two figures above. It repeats the
                                 word because a screen reader cannot see the tint and has no other way
                                 to learn that a figure is short rather than merely different.

                                 The tint is a BINDING now. It was a DataTrigger Setter holding a bare
                                 {StaticResource Danger}, and a trigger's Setter takes a value rather
                                 than a binding expression, so that token was resolved once at parse
                                 time and stayed the light one in dark theme: Danger #D32F2F on
                                 BackgroundDark #121212 is 3.76:1, against 9.40:1 for DangerDark on
                                 the same surface. ShiftAnalyticsViewModel.DifferenceColor resolves it
                                 against the live theme, and names the label's own default ink for the
                                 balanced case so this looks exactly as it did. -->
                            <Label Text="{Binding DifferenceText}" FontSize="18" FontAttributes="Bold"
                                   TextColor="{Binding DifferenceColor}"
                                   SemanticProperties.Description="{Binding DifferenceHint}" />
                            <Label Text="{Binding ReasonText, StringFormat='Причина: {0}'}" Style="{StaticResource SecondaryLabel}"
                                   IsVisible="{Binding HasReason}" LineBreakMode="WordWrap" />
                            <!-- Stale: the ledger moved AFTER the count. Shown as its own paragraph with
                                 both figures, because it answers a different question from the one
                                 above — "did the cashier err at close" and "are the books right now"
                                 deliberately have different answers. -->
                            <BoxView HeightRequest="1" Margin="0,4,0,2" Color="{AppThemeBinding Light={StaticResource Gray300}, Dark={StaticResource Gray700}}" IsVisible="{Binding IsReconciliationStale}" />
                            <Label Text="Учёт изменился после пересчёта" FontAttributes="Bold" IsVisible="{Binding IsReconciliationStale}" />
                            <Label Text="{Binding StaleText}" Style="{StaticResource SecondaryLabel}"
                                   IsVisible="{Binding IsReconciliationStale}" LineBreakMode="WordWrap"
                                   SemanticProperties.Description="{Binding StaleHint}" />
                        </VerticalStackLayout>
                    </Border>
                </VerticalStackLayout>
                <!-- ═══ THE FILTER / SORT / GROUP PANEL ═══
                     One trigger row, CLOSED by default. The breakdown is at the bottom of a long
                     scrolling page, and the manager who opens this screen wants the shift's figures,
                     not a search box. Everything the panel holds is also stated on the trigger
                     itself, so a collapsed panel is never ambiguous. -->
                <Border Grid.Row="5" Style="{StaticResource CardBorder}">
                    <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="8">
                        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto">
                            <Grid.GestureRecognizers>
                                <TapGestureRecognizer Command="{Binding ToggleFilterPanelCommand}" />
                            </Grid.GestureRecognizers>
                            <VerticalStackLayout>
                                <Label Text="Фильтры и сортировка" FontAttributes="Bold" />
                                <Label Text="{Binding FilterPanelSummary}" Style="{StaticResource SecondaryLabel}"
                                       LineBreakMode="WordWrap"
                                       SemanticProperties.Description="{Binding FilterPanelHint}" />
                            </VerticalStackLayout>
                            <Label Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding FilterPanelGlyph}" FontSize="18"
                                   VerticalTextAlignment="Center" Margin="8,0,0,0" />
                        </Grid>

                        <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="10" IsVisible="{Binding IsFilterPanelOpen}">
                            <!-- SECTIONS. A horizontal strip rather than a Picker, because a Picker
                                 opens a blocking modal on Android and cannot show the active filter
                                 as part of the list header — the reason the catalogue page moved off
                                 it in the first place. Multi-select, so «Все» is expressed by
                                 un-checking every chip (an empty set) rather than by a sentinel. -->
                            <Label Text="Разделы" Style="{StaticResource Caption}" />
                            <!-- NO negative margin. The orders board's chip strip bleeds 12dp to the screen edge because
                                 it sits on the page background; this one sits inside a bordered card,
                                 and pulling the scroller past the card's own left edge made the
                                 ScrollView's clip cut the FIRST chip in half — «по разделам и
                                 блюдам» rendered as «елам и блюдам». The card's padding is the
                                 correct inset and the strip still scrolls. -->
                            <ScrollView Orientation="Horizontal" HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Never"
                                        HeightRequest="44">
                                <HorizontalStackLayout BindableLayout.ItemsSource="{Binding SectionChips}"
                                                        Spacing="0">
                                    <BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                                        <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:ProductAnalyticsSectionChip">
                                            <Border Style="{StaticResource FilterChip}" Margin="0,0,8,0">
                                                <Border.Triggers>
                                                    <DataTrigger TargetType="Border" Binding="{Binding IsSelected}" Value="True">
                                                        <Setter Property="BackgroundColor" Value="{StaticResource Primary}" />
                                                        <Setter Property="Stroke" Value="Transparent" />
                                                    </DataTrigger>
                                                </Border.Triggers>
                                                <Label Text="{Binding Label}" Style="{StaticResource FilterChipText}"
                                                       SemanticProperties.Description="{Binding Hint}">
                                                    <Label.Triggers>
                                                        <DataTrigger TargetType="Label" Binding="{Binding IsSelected}" Value="True">
                                                            <Setter Property="TextColor" Value="White" />
                                                        </DataTrigger>
                                                    </Label.Triggers>
                                                </Label>
                                                <Border.GestureRecognizers>
                                                    <TapGestureRecognizer
                                                        Command="{Binding Source={RelativeSource AncestorType={x:Type ContentPage}}, Path=BindingContext.SelectSectionChipCommand}"
                                                        CommandParameter="{Binding .}" />
                                                </Border.GestureRecognizers>
                                            </Border>
                                        </DataTemplate>
                                    </BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                                </HorizontalStackLayout>
                            </ScrollView>

                            <!-- An Entry, NOT a SearchBar: SearchBar is drawn by the platform and
                                 looks different on Windows and Android, so the one control every
                                 screen should look identical on is the one that does not. The
                                 cross is a sibling of the field, not inside it — Button.Content
                                 cannot hold arbitrary controls. -->
                            <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto">
                                <Entry Style="{StaticResource FormField}"
                                       Placeholder="Поиск по названию блюда"
                                       Text="{Binding SearchText}"
                                       SemanticProperties.Description="Поиск по названию блюда" />
                                <Button Grid.Column="1" Text="✕" Margin="8,0,0,0"
                                        Command="{Binding ClearSearchCommand}"
                                        IsVisible="{Binding HasSearch}"
                                        SemanticProperties.Description="Очистить поиск" />
                            </Grid>

                            <!-- GROUPING. Three chips, three shapes. The default is the two-level
                                 «по разделам и блюдам» because that is the question a manager asks
                                 of a section report; «без группировки» is here because the flat list
                                 is what this screen always showed and a reader looking for it should
                                 not have to be told it no longer exists. -->
                            <Label Text="Группировка" Style="{StaticResource Caption}" />
                            <!-- The scroller is not decoration. A bare HorizontalStackLayout clips at
                                 the page width and silently drops everything past the fold: «без
                                 группировки» was simply unreachable on a 411dp phone, with no way to
                                 tell it existed. Same fix as the orders board's chip strip. -->
                            <ScrollView Orientation="Horizontal" HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Never"
                                        HeightRequest="44">
                                <HorizontalStackLayout BindableLayout.ItemsSource="{Binding GroupingOptions}"
                                                        Spacing="0">
                                    <BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                                        <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:ProductAnalyticsGroupingOption">
                                            <Border Style="{StaticResource FilterChip}" Margin="0,0,8,0">
                                                <Border.Triggers>
                                                    <DataTrigger TargetType="Border" Binding="{Binding IsSelected}" Value="True">
                                                        <Setter Property="BackgroundColor" Value="{StaticResource Primary}" />
                                                        <Setter Property="Stroke" Value="Transparent" />
                                                    </DataTrigger>
                                                </Border.Triggers>
                                                <Label Text="{Binding Name}" Style="{StaticResource FilterChipText}"
                                                       SemanticProperties.Description="{Binding Hint}">
                                                    <Label.Triggers>
                                                        <DataTrigger TargetType="Label" Binding="{Binding IsSelected}" Value="True">
                                                            <Setter Property="TextColor" Value="White" />
                                                        </DataTrigger>
                                                    </Label.Triggers>
                                                </Label>
                                                <Border.GestureRecognizers>
                                                    <TapGestureRecognizer
                                                        Command="{Binding Source={RelativeSource AncestorType={x:Type ContentPage}}, Path=BindingContext.SelectGroupingCommand}"
                                                        CommandParameter="{Binding .}" />
                                                </Border.GestureRecognizers>
                                            </Border>
                                        </DataTemplate>
                                    </BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                                </HorizontalStackLayout>
                            </ScrollView>

                            <!-- SORTING. One strip of criteria plus one direction button, and the
                                 button is separate for a reason: re-picking the criterion already in
                                 force REVERSES it (see SelectSort), so the two affordances overlap
                                 and the explicit button is what makes the current direction
                                 visible at a glance instead of implied. -->
                            <Label Text="Сортировка" Style="{StaticResource Caption}" />
                            <!-- Scroller for the same reason as the grouping strip above: «по
                                 названию» is the longest criterion and lands past the fold. -->
                            <ScrollView Orientation="Horizontal" HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Never"
                                        HeightRequest="44">
                                <HorizontalStackLayout BindableLayout.ItemsSource="{Binding SortOptions}" Spacing="0">
                                    <BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                                        <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:ProductAnalyticsSortOption">
                                            <Border Style="{StaticResource FilterChip}" Margin="0,0,8,0">
                                                <Border.Triggers>
                                                    <DataTrigger TargetType="Border" Binding="{Binding IsSelected}" Value="True">
                                                        <Setter Property="BackgroundColor" Value="{StaticResource Primary}" />
                                                        <Setter Property="Stroke" Value="Transparent" />
                                                    </DataTrigger>
                                                </Border.Triggers>
                                                <Label Text="{Binding Name}" Style="{StaticResource FilterChipText}"
                                                       SemanticProperties.Description="{Binding Hint}">
                                                    <Label.Triggers>
                                                        <DataTrigger TargetType="Label" Binding="{Binding IsSelected}" Value="True">
                                                            <Setter Property="TextColor" Value="White" />
                                                        </DataTrigger>
                                                    </Label.Triggers>
                                                </Label>
                                                <Border.GestureRecognizers>
                                                    <TapGestureRecognizer
                                                        Command="{Binding Source={RelativeSource AncestorType={x:Type ContentPage}}, Path=BindingContext.SelectSortCommand}"
                                                        CommandParameter="{Binding .}" />
                                                </Border.GestureRecognizers>
                                            </Border>
                                        </DataTemplate>
                                    </BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                                </HorizontalStackLayout>
                            </ScrollView>
                            <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto">
                                <Label Text="{Binding SortDirectionName}" VerticalTextAlignment="Center" />
                                <Button Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding SortDirectionGlyph}"
                                        Command="{Binding ToggleSortDirectionCommand}"
                                        SemanticProperties.Description="{Binding SortDirectionHint}" />
                            </Grid>
                        </VerticalStackLayout>
                    </VerticalStackLayout>
                </Border>

                <!-- Heading is no longer a constant. «Продажи по блюдам и модификаторам» became a lie
                     the moment a section header went above a modifier row. -->
                <Label Grid.Row="6" Text="{Binding ProductSectionTitle}" Style="{StaticResource SectionTitle}" />

                <!-- The summary the cards above cannot give: they do not move when the list is
                     filtered, so without this line a two-row list under «Продано позиций 137» looks
                     like the app lost data. ABOVE the list, not below — under it, the reader has to
                     scroll past everything to find the answer to "why is this short". -->
                <Label Grid.Row="7" Text="{Binding VisibleSummaryText}" Style="{StaticResource SecondaryLabel}"
                       IsVisible="{Binding HasVisibleSummary}" LineBreakMode="WordWrap"
                       SemanticProperties.Description="{Binding VisibleSummaryHint}" />

                <!-- ═══ THE THREE SHAPES ═══
                     One scroller, one gesture, and each list measures itself — the trade-off is
                     spelled out at the top of this file. Nothing here recycles: it is bounded by the
                     distinct products sold in ONE shift. -->

                <!-- 1. SECTIONS → DISHES → MODIFIERS. The default. -->
                <VerticalStackLayout Grid.Row="8" Spacing="0"
                                     BindableLayout.ItemsSource="{Binding SectionRows}"
                                     IsVisible="{Binding IsSectionGrouping}">
                    <BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                        <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:ProductAnalyticsSectionRow">
                            <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="0">
                                <Border Style="{StaticResource CardBorder}"
                                        BackgroundColor="{AppThemeBinding Light={StaticResource Gray100}, Dark={StaticResource Gray800}}">
                                    <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto">
                                        <VerticalStackLayout>
                                            <Label Text="{Binding Name}" FontAttributes="Bold" />
                                            <Label Text="{Binding Share}" Style="{StaticResource CountLabel}" />
                                        </VerticalStackLayout>
                                        <VerticalStackLayout Grid.Column="1" HorizontalOptions="End">
                                            <Label Text="{Binding QuantityText}" HorizontalTextAlignment="End" />
                                            <Label Text="{Binding RevenueText}" FontAttributes="Bold"
                                                   HorizontalTextAlignment="End" />
                                        </VerticalStackLayout>
                                    </Grid>
                                </Border>
                                <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="0"
                                                     BindableLayout.ItemsSource="{Binding Dishes}"
                                                     Margin="12,0,0,0">
                                    <BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                                        <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:ProductAnalyticsDishRow">
                                            <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="0">
                                                <Border Style="{StaticResource CardBorderCompact}">
                                                    <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*,Auto">
                                                        <Grid.GestureRecognizers>
                                                            <TapGestureRecognizer
                                                                Command="{Binding Source={RelativeSource AncestorType={x:Type ContentPage}}, Path=BindingContext.ToggleDishCommand}"
                                                                CommandParameter="{Binding .}" />
                                                        </Grid.GestureRecognizers>
                                                        <!-- The chevron is TEXT, not an image asset, and the
                                                             fold state is also in the row's
                                                             description: a glyph alone is invisible
                                                             to a screen reader, which would then have
                                                             no way to tell a folded dish from a dish
                                                             with nothing under it. -->
                                                        <Label Text="{Binding ChevronGlyph}" FontSize="16"
                                                               WidthRequest="20" VerticalTextAlignment="Center"
                                                               HorizontalTextAlignment="Center" />
                                                        <VerticalStackLayout Grid.Column="1">
                                                            <Label Text="{Binding Name}" FontAttributes="Bold" />
                                                            <Label Text="{Binding Share}" Style="{StaticResource CountLabel}" />
                                                        </VerticalStackLayout>
                                                        <VerticalStackLayout Grid.Column="2" HorizontalOptions="End">
                                                            <Label Text="{Binding QuantityText}" HorizontalTextAlignment="End" />
                                                            <Label Text="{Binding RevenueText}" FontAttributes="Bold"
                                                                   HorizontalTextAlignment="End" />
                                                        </VerticalStackLayout>
                                                    </Grid>
                                                </Border>
                                                <!-- A folded dish costs its rows nothing: a collapsed
                                                     child in a VerticalStackLayout is neither measured
                                                     nor counted for spacing (see the note at the top of
                                                     this file), so IsVisible is the whole mechanism. -->
                                                <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="0"
                                                                     BindableLayout.ItemsSource="{Binding Lines}"
                                                                     IsVisible="{Binding IsExpanded}"
                                                                     Margin="20,0,0,0">
                                                    <BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                                                        <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:ProductAnalyticsLineRow">
                                                            <Border Style="{StaticResource CardBorderCompact}"
                                                                    BackgroundColor="Transparent"
                                                                    Stroke="Transparent"
                                                                    Padding="8,4"
                                                                    SemanticProperties.Description="{Binding Hint}">
                                                                <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto,Auto" ColumnSpacing="10">
                                                                    <Label Text="{Binding ModifierName}"
                                                                           Style="{StaticResource SecondaryLabel}"
                                                                           LineBreakMode="TailTruncation" />
                                                                    <Label Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding Quantity, StringFormat='× {0}'}"
                                                                           Style="{StaticResource SecondaryLabel}"
                                                                           HorizontalTextAlignment="End" />
                                                                    <Label Grid.Column="2" Text="{Binding RevenueText}"
                                                                           Style="{StaticResource SecondaryLabel}"
                                                                           HorizontalTextAlignment="End" />
                                                                </Grid>
                                                                <!-- The description rides on the LINE's own Border,
                                                                     not on the dish header above it: a container
                                                                     with a contentDescription is announced as
                                                                     one node and its children are not traversed,
                                                                     so putting it higher would swallow every
                                                                     modifier row under it. -->
                                                            </Border>
                                                        </DataTemplate>
                                                    </BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                                                </VerticalStackLayout>
                                            </VerticalStackLayout>
                                        </DataTemplate>
                                    </BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                                </VerticalStackLayout>
                            </VerticalStackLayout>
                        </DataTemplate>
                    </BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                </VerticalStackLayout>

                <!-- 2. DISHES → MODIFIERS. No section level. -->
                <VerticalStackLayout Grid.Row="8" Spacing="0"
                                     BindableLayout.ItemsSource="{Binding DishRows}"
                                     IsVisible="{Binding IsDishGrouping}">
                    <BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                        <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:ProductAnalyticsDishRow">
                            <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="0">
                                <Border Style="{StaticResource CardBorder}"
                                        BackgroundColor="{AppThemeBinding Light={StaticResource Gray100}, Dark={StaticResource Gray800}}">
                                    <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*,Auto">
                                        <Grid.GestureRecognizers>
                                            <TapGestureRecognizer
                                                Command="{Binding Source={RelativeSource AncestorType={x:Type ContentPage}}, Path=BindingContext.ToggleDishCommand}"
                                                CommandParameter="{Binding .}" />
                                        </Grid.GestureRecognizers>
                                        <Label Text="{Binding ChevronGlyph}" FontSize="16"
                                               WidthRequest="20" VerticalTextAlignment="Center"
                                               HorizontalTextAlignment="Center" />
                                        <VerticalStackLayout Grid.Column="1">
                                            <Label Text="{Binding Name}" FontAttributes="Bold" />
                                            <Label Text="{Binding Share}" Style="{StaticResource CountLabel}" />
                                        </VerticalStackLayout>
                                        <VerticalStackLayout Grid.Column="2" HorizontalOptions="End">
                                            <Label Text="{Binding QuantityText}" HorizontalTextAlignment="End" />
                                            <Label Text="{Binding RevenueText}" FontAttributes="Bold"
                                                   HorizontalTextAlignment="End" />
                                        </VerticalStackLayout>
                                    </Grid>
                                    </Border>
                                <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="0"
                                                     BindableLayout.ItemsSource="{Binding Lines}"
                                                     IsVisible="{Binding IsExpanded}"
                                                     Margin="20,0,0,0">
                                    <BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                                        <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:ProductAnalyticsLineRow">
                                            <Border Style="{StaticResource CardBorderCompact}"
                                                    BackgroundColor="Transparent" Stroke="Transparent"
                                                    Padding="8,4"
                                                    SemanticProperties.Description="{Binding Hint}">
                                                <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto,Auto" ColumnSpacing="10">
                                                    <Label Text="{Binding ModifierName}"
                                                           Style="{StaticResource SecondaryLabel}"
                                                           LineBreakMode="TailTruncation" />
                                                    <Label Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding Quantity, StringFormat='× {0}'}"
                                                           Style="{StaticResource SecondaryLabel}"
                                                           HorizontalTextAlignment="End" />
                                                    <Label Grid.Column="2" Text="{Binding RevenueText}"
                                                           Style="{StaticResource SecondaryLabel}"
                                                           HorizontalTextAlignment="End" />
                                                </Grid>
                                            </Border>
                                        </DataTemplate>
                                    </BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                                </VerticalStackLayout>
                            </VerticalStackLayout>
                        </DataTemplate>
                    </BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                </VerticalStackLayout>

                <!-- 3. FLAT. Exactly the list this screen had before: one row per dish × modifier. -->
                <VerticalStackLayout Grid.Row="8" BindableLayout.ItemsSource="{Binding LineRows}" Spacing="0"
                                     IsVisible="{Binding IsFlatGrouping}">
                    <BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                        <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:ProductAnalyticsLineRow">
                            <Border Style="{StaticResource CardBorder}">
                                <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto" RowDefinitions="Auto,Auto">
                                    <Label Text="{Binding ProductName}" FontAttributes="Bold" />
                                    <Label Grid.Row="1" Text="{Binding ModifierName}" Style="{StaticResource SecondaryLabel}" />
                                    <VerticalStackLayout Grid.Column="1" Grid.RowSpan="2" HorizontalOptions="End">
                                        <Label Text="{Binding Quantity, StringFormat='× {0}'}" HorizontalTextAlignment="End" />
                                        <Label Text="{Binding RevenueText}" FontAttributes="Bold" HorizontalTextAlignment="End" />
                                    </VerticalStackLayout>
                                </Grid>
                            </Border>
                        </DataTemplate>
                    </BindableLayout.ItemTemplate>
                </VerticalStackLayout>

                <!-- One sentence for THREE situations, which is why it is bound to a computed
                     property rather than written out: a shift with no closed orders, a filter that
                     excluded everything and a search that matched nothing are different facts, and
                     the single hardcoded string this label used to carry could only state the
                     first. BindableLayout has no EmptyView, hence a label. -->
                <Label Grid.Row="9" Text="{Binding EmptyListText}" Style="{StaticResource EmptyLabel}"
                       IsVisible="{Binding HasNoProductRows}" />
        </Grid>
    </ScrollView>
</ContentPage>
